note bulletin Storm bulletin | HARBOR AUTHORITY - STORM BULLETIN\n\nGale tonight. Shutters down on every roof. The alarm bell on the Authority's roof to be rung when it breaks.\n\nThe council meets in the storm, as the law says. The Authority, the Fleet and the Union will each be heard.
note authdemand Authority demand | THE AUTHORITY'S DEMAND\n\nThe water stays with those who keep the pumps. The Fleet's smuggling ends. The Union's tenth is raised to a fifth.\n\nOrder keeps the city dry.
note fleetdemand Fleet demand | THE FREE FLEET'S DEMAND\n\nThe pumps to the boats that carry the water. The Authority's permits burned. The boom open, day and night.\n\nThe sea belongs to those who sail it.
note uniondemand Union demand | THE UNION'S DEMAND\n\nThe Union's divers brought up every pump in this city. The pumps are ours by salvage law.\n\nWhat we bring up, we share - with the Union.
note authsecret Authority secret | Sealed with the Authority's anchor -\n\nCouncillor Crane: the countersignatures on the valve log are in your own hand. The Fleet and the Union never signed. But they have both taken our money since, to keep quiet, so now they can never say so without drowning with us. If this comes out, all three go down together. Keep the code safe: it starts 4.
note fleetsecret Fleet secret | Sealed with the Fleet's gull -\n\nTeo: we took the Authority's money after the valves. The boats needed fuel. We knew that signature wasn't yours, and we let it stand. The Rookery will never know. The code's middle: 7 then 1.
note unionsecret Union secret | Sealed with the Union's hook -\n\nForeman: Crane's man brought the money the week Marlowe's team went down. You swore at him, and then you took it for the widows' fund. If Ines talks, we are finished as well as him. The code ends 9.
note letters Faction letters | The factions' letters for the council, sealed and stacked - one each, and none of them meant for you.
note fiveways Five ways | FIVE WAYS THE CITY CAN GO\n\nTHE AUTHORITY - order, and the water stays theirs.\nTHE FLEET - the pumps go to the boats.\nTHE UNION - salvage law; the cranes rule.\nEXPOSE - read the valve log and the ledger page aloud; let the city judge all three.\nFREE - the water goes to the Rookery, and the Rookery leaves for a shoal of its own.\n\nPull one lever. The council will hear only one.
note verdictauthority The verdict | THE AUTHORITY KEEPS THE WATER.\n\nThe pumps stay locked. The streets stay quiet. In the Rookery the barrels stay empty, and nobody asks why.\n\nBut when the vote is counted, the Councillor is not in his chair. His coat is on the back of it, soaked through.
note verdictfleet The verdict | THE FLEET TAKES THE PUMPS.\n\nBoats come and go through an open boom. The water flows - to whoever has a boat.
note verdictunion The verdict | THE UNION RUNS THE WATER.\n\nThe cranes turn day and night. Every barrel filled is chalked, every chalk mark paid.
note verdictexpose The verdict | ALL THREE EXPOSED.\n\nThe valve log is read in every market. The councillor runs, the Fleet's captains scatter, the foreman resigns. The city will have to start again.
note verdictfree The verdict | THE ROOKERY GOES FREE.\n\nThe Rookery's barrels are filled from the Authority's tanks, and at dawn its boats leave for a shoal of their own, ahead of you across the water.
note teomsg Teo Varga's message | Left on the council table, in the Fleet's chalk -\n\nWhatever you chose, it's chosen. I won't argue it. The valves were never my shame - the money was, and that's said now.\n\nCrane didn't stay for the vote. Nell saw him go: out the back in his shirtsleeves, into the storm, down the pile stair with a lantern. Whatever he's been carrying all these years, he's gone to carry it alone.\n\nThe piles are groaning. If they go, the Crown goes, and every roof with it - the Rookery's too. Somebody has to follow him down. I can't dive. You can.\n\n- Teo Varga
note pilemap Pile engineer's map | THE FOUNDATION PILES\n\nThe whole crown stands on four piles. The storm has cracked them. Jack them up, one by one, or the city goes down tonight.\n\nThe pile stair on the key's shore goes down to the first pile head.\n\n(Fresh, in wet pencil: Jacks one to four, in order. Do not let anyone wind number four alone. - pile engineer, retired, who should have said this louder)
note councilchest Council reward | The council's reward, for the one who spoke.
loot letters Rope*2
prop letters loot.refill=0
loot councilchest TradeToken*10;MetalIngot*4;CircuitBoard*2
prop councilchest loot.refill=0

